{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 992adea2: a pure catalog-vocabulary owner below Platform. Do not extend the platform or admission ports, and do not change the named-pin provider contract.\n\nReason: BR-13's acceptance is that the golden table of every pin against each question passes unchanged. A port that requires answer metadata refuses stand-ins that are accepted today, which changes behavior. A duplicate literal list keeps the debt. One table that every layer can import does neither.\n\nShape:\n1. One module of data and predicates with no imports. It holds the per-pin answers for the questions that derive/src/program/body.ts, git/src/archive-policy.ts and any other layer below Platform ask.\n2. Place it in the lowest existing package that derive, git and platform all depend on already. Add no workspace package. If no such package exists, stop and report the dependency graph before you create one.\n3. packages/platform re-exports the module and stays the owner that code above Platform asks. Code below Platform imports the module directly. Each question has one table row set, in one file.\n4. No compatibility adapter. The named-pin stand-ins stay as they are, and absent metadata still grants nothing new.\n\nI amend the acceptance sentence of 487496f5 to match: code outside packages/platform asks the catalog, or for a layer below Platform the catalog's vocabulary module, for named capabilities. The golden table now has 105 questions with the `isStandingDestination` predicate and passes unchanged. No list is unified. Record each disagreement between lists as its own named question, as you do.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}